From 27cd0bd05d45cccb71bb1b8887c3c761d9397f9b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Jeong, Heon" <blmarket@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 23 Aug 2026 16:55:25 -0700
Subject: Fix memory leak when destroying pane

r.ranges field should be freed when destroying pane. A pane that writes
output makes the server work out which of its columns are not obscured,
and the ranges builder grows the pane's own struct visible_ranges r
through server_client_ensure_ranges(). The other owners of one give the
array back -- tty_free() frees tty->r.ranges, popup_free_cb() frees
pd->r.ranges and menu_free_cb() frees md->r.ranges -- but the pane's was
never freed, so every pane the server destroys loses one allocation.

A server that makes and destroys 20 panes, each printing a line, exits
under AddressSanitizer with

    Direct leak of 160 byte(s) in 20 object(s) allocated from:
        #1 xrecallocarray xmalloc.c:80
        #2 server_client_ensure_ranges server-client.c:160
        #3 window_visible_ranges window-visible.c:91
        #4 screen_write_collect_flush_line screen-write.c:2344
        #5 screen_write_collect_flush screen-write.c:2444
        #6 screen_write_stop screen-write.c:414
        #7 input_parse_pane input.c:1038
        #8 window_pane_read_callback window.c:1586

one block per destroyed pane, and none with this applied.

Ported to 3.7b: upstream splits the teardown into window_pane_destroy and
window_pane_free and the free belongs to the latter; 3.7b has only
window_pane_destroy. The builder is screen_redraw_get_visible_ranges()
here rather than window_visible_ranges(), and it reaches
server_client_ensure_ranges(&wp->r, ...) the same way.
---
 window.c | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/window.c b/window.c
--- a/window.c
+++ b/window.c
@@ -1108,6 +1108,8 @@ window_pane_destroy(struct window_pane *wp)
 
 	screen_free(&wp->base);
 
+	free(wp->r.ranges);
+
 	if (wp->pipe_fd != -1) {
 		bufferevent_free(wp->pipe_event);
 		close(wp->pipe_fd);
